  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "Except in some very rare cases, the card each player draws will be the card revealed from the top of their library.",
      "oracle_id": "8ee2dd43-cda2-4cb7-9e4b-1946d5b7467e",
      "published_at": "2014-05-29",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If Selvala’s Enforcer leaves the battlefield before its ability resolves, the top card of each library will still be revealed and drawn, although no +1/+1 counters will be placed.",
      "oracle_id": "8ee2dd43-cda2-4cb7-9e4b-1946d5b7467e",
      "published_at": "2014-05-29",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Dredge can replace any card draw, not only the one during your draw step.",
      "oracle_id": "ac8fba34-512c-4f24-999a-ab72f1ce4acb",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an effect puts a card into your hand without specifically using the word \"draw,\" you're not drawing a card. Dredge can't replace this event.",
      "oracle_id": "ac8fba34-512c-4f24-999a-ab72f1ce4acb",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you're drawing multiple cards, each draw is performed one at a time. For example, if you're instructed to draw two cards and you replace the first draw with a dredge ability, another card with a dredge ability (including one that was milled by the first dredge ability) may be used to replace the second draw.",
      "oracle_id": "ac8fba34-512c-4f24-999a-ab72f1ce4acb",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once you've announced that you're applying a card's dredge ability to replace a draw, players can't take any actions until you've put that card into your hand and milled cards.",
      "oracle_id": "ac8fba34-512c-4f24-999a-ab72f1ce4acb",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "One card draw can't be replaced by multiple dredge abilities.",
      "oracle_id": "ac8fba34-512c-4f24-999a-ab72f1ce4acb",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can't attempt to use a dredge ability if you don't have enough cards in your library.",
      "oracle_id": "ac8fba34-512c-4f24-999a-ab72f1ce4acb",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Except in some very rare cases, the card each player draws will be the card revealed from the top of their library.",
      "oracle_id": "b265ac18-3923-46ba-b7b6-4190855815e1",
      "published_at": "2014-05-29",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Except in some very rare cases, the card each player draws will be the card revealed from the top of their library.",
      "oracle_id": "b628a39b-c923-473d-900a-1617f47ecb76",
      "published_at": "2014-05-29",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you activate Selvala's ability while casting a spell, and you discover you can't produce enough mana to pay that spell's costs, the spell is reversed. The spell returns to whatever zone you were casting it from. You may reverse other mana abilities you activated while casting the spell, but Selvala's ability can't be reversed. You'll still have whatever mana that ability produced, and each player will have drawn a card.",
      "oracle_id": "b628a39b-c923-473d-900a-1617f47ecb76",
      "published_at": "2014-05-29",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Selvala's parley ability is a mana ability. It doesn't use the stack and can't be responded to.",
      "oracle_id": "b628a39b-c923-473d-900a-1617f47ecb76",
      "published_at": "2014-05-29",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Except in some very rare cases, the card each player draws will be the card revealed from the top of their library.",
      "oracle_id": "e5e42293-ce01-4872-be2a-a79ff4312992",
      "published_at": "2014-05-29",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
